the PlayStation 4 had a strong 2015 two  years into its lifecycle it remains  ahead of its competitors in terms of  sales and boasts an impressive library  spanning every genre within our  embarrassment of riches here are the  games GameSpot calls the best of the  best PlayStation 4 hit the ground  running in 2015 with blood-borne our  highest voted exclusive for the console  it hit the sweet spot for many souls  fans and reeled in those who had never  played from software's dark fantasy  games drenched in gore and colored by  darkness blood-borne stole our time with  a comfortable and accessible combat  system a never-ending stream of  challenging combat encounters and an  expertly crafted narrative that  unraveled slowly and suddenly a home -  yeah  we're always spurred on by the bits of  lore we find always eager to see what's  lurking behind every corner always  pushing ahead despite the constant  threat just one more gathering of blood  echoes just one more attempt at a boss  we've been salivating for fallout 4 is  post-apocalyptic world since rumours  first spread of its existence and once  it was in our hands it did not  disappoint the wasteland is dreary  enriched with thrifty traders and  hideous foes you help or hinder other  wastelanders kill death claws and other  gruesome beasts for its supplies meet  survivors and generally work your way to  becoming the wasteland Savior it's a  rollercoaster of an experience made even  more enjoyable by deep crafting and  settlement building systems that allow  you to leave your own personal mark on  the wasteland it's easy to get lost  literally and fallout 4 is dilapidated  irradiated version of Boston but fallout  4 isn't the only all-consuming  open-world adventure on ps4 this year  The Witcher 3 Wild Hunt dropped you into  a lush vibrant fantasy land into the  shoes of infamous monster hunter Geralt  of Rivia Geralt mission is personal in  his story poignant as are the side  quests and intertwined plot lines  throughout the game The Witcher threes  world is just beautiful and so are its  stories romance and companions resolving  other's heartbreak and searching for and  protecting your loved ones are how  you'll spend your time wild hence world  has also been supported by an excellent  mansion hearts of stone the perfect  addition for those of us who want more  after completing every inch of content  in the main game in this we acknowledge  The Witcher 3 as one of the best of the  best on PlayStation 4 unearthing the  mysteries and lore of Metal Gear Solid 5  the phantom pain provided one of our  favorite things to do this year even if  you know nothing of Metal Gear the  phantom pain story of sacrifice and loss  is a powerful one and forms the  foundation of its complex yet engaging  world whether you're running into combat  with d-dog or quiet just spending some  time building up mother base or folding  animals there's never a dull moment  adding to the potency to paint and paint  is that it's a send-off for Metal Gear  creator Hideo Kojima it is evident that  his heart and soul went into this game  efforts have been worth it  the phantom pain leaves a lasting  impression on us that we won't be quick  to forget rounding up ps4 is best is  indeed darling rocket League it came  seemingly out of nowhere rocket league  launched with very little PR hype or  fanfare on its initial release and yet  without marketing guidance players  discovered in some countless hours into  matches something about using cars to  boot giant balls around a soccer field  is addicting and we constantly feel  challenged to do better execute better  tricks and master the game and a  plethora of small flourishes give rocket  league an undeniable charm putting a hat  on the car making rainbows come out of  your exhaust pipe or having the flag of  your country wobbling around as you tear  across the field it's the game of choice  for our staffs multiplayer sessions we  love rocket leagues perfect little  package because it connects us with each  other in meaningful challenges when a  team comes together for that one magical  moment where you carry a ball across an  area bouncing between teammates and off  the ceiling and walls then into the net  it's undeniably satisfying it takes  common videogame elements and matches  them together into something totally  tantalizing the news  to those who haven't purchased a ps4 yet  with a best of list like this one it's  difficult to say that the purchase isn't  worth it and to those who already have  one we hope you like us get the chance  to enjoy these games as much as we do  you
 

